# Critical Thinking

## Objective

Do not accept the first plausible answer  -  evaluate correctness, risks, and alternatives.

## Requirements

- Question whether the change solves the real problem.
- Consider failure modes and edge cases.
- Compare at least one alternative when the decision is significant.
- Separate facts from inference.

